      "Then keep things in proportion. A rented helmet sits on your head six hours a day; the basin gets one. Lice move head to head, and public health agencies describe transfer by comb, hat or towel as uncommon. The herbal decoction poured over you simmered for fifteen to thirty minutes, which clears that 60-degree line by a wide margin. What money does not buy is sterility: the 120K to 350K short wash and the 450K to 900K ritual share one trolley."
