          "Two other small things. Have the blow-dry sitting up instead of standing, and take a minute at the door before you walk into the heat, because getting up fast after an hour of warm reclining is how a grey-out starts in anybody. Watch the air conditioning as well: in a Da Nang spa room it is often aimed straight down at the beds and set to 24 degrees while the street sits at 33. <em>Tránh gió điều hòa nhé</em> asks them to point it elsewhere.",
          "Four things end the session early: dizziness or feeling faint, nausea that comes on while you are lying down, a pounding or fluttering heart, and shortness of breath. If any one of them appears, sit up; that usually fixes it within a minute because it undoes the compression, and <em>mình thấy choáng, cho mình ngồi lên</em> is the whole sentence. For anything that does not resolve, Da Nang uses 115 as its single citywide emergency number. The city's maternity hospital, Bệnh viện Phụ sản - Nhi Đà Nẵng, is at 402 Lê Văn Hiến in Ngũ Hành Sơn, on 0236 395 7777, about ten minutes from the beach-side spa cluster, and it is the site to go to for anything urgent. Its second premises at 26C Chu Văn An in Hải Châu takes low-risk appointments only and sends emergencies to the main hospital."
